ENNX

Build

    bazel build //:wheel --config=release

The Bazel wheel is written to Bazel's output tree and targets CPython 3.13.
GitHub Releases, not PyPI, distribute CPython 3.12 through 3.14 platform
wheels built with Buck2. Install the wheel matching the target Python ABI and
platform directly from its release asset.

CUDA wheels are built and parity-checked on a T4, then attached to the same
release with:

    ./ennx release upload vX.Y.Z PATH/TO/ennx-*.whl

Test

    bazel test //:check //:audit --config=release --config=constrained

See docs/testing.md for the test tiers, generated-workload policy, and
hardware/benchmark gates.

See docs/colab.md for the hosted T4 CUDA development workflow.

See docs/api.md for the stable, experimental, and internal API boundary.

Format

    bazel run @buildifier_prebuilt//:buildifier -- -r .

Targets

    //:cpu      CPU implementation
    //:gpu      platform GPU implementation
    //:wheel    Python wheel
    //:check    test suite
    //:audit    wheel audit

See docs/bazel.md for dependency and platform details.
